  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dinesh vs State Of Haryana on 28 August, 2024 Author: Pankaj Jain Bench: Pankaj Jain Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:111096 Crm-M-40626-2024 1 219 In The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana At Chandigarh Crm-M-40626-2024 Date of decision : 28.08.2024 Dinesh ....Petitioner Versus State Of Haryana ...Respondent Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Pankaj Jain Present : Mr. Bijender S. Dhankhar, Advocate for the petitioner. Mr. Apurv Garg, Sr. DAG, Haryana. PANKAJ JAIN, J. (ORAL) This petition has been filed under Section 439 Cr.P.C. for grant of regular bail to the petitioner in case F.I.R. No.124 dated 21.02.2021 registered for the offences punishable under Sections 120-B, 148, 186, 302, 332, 353, 379B/149 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (Section 379B of IPC added later on) and Section 45 of the Prisons Act, 1894 at Police Station City, Sonipat, District Sonipat. Sd/- Ankit Malik, D.S.P., District Jail, Sonipat (Ankit Malik)\" Details of pending cases against the petitioner as mentioned in the custody certificate are tabulated as under: Sr. FIR No. Date of FIR Police Station Offences No. Under Section 1 568/2022 04.10.2022 City Jagadhri, Yamuna 42-A of Prisons Act Nagar 2 580/2011 N/A Partapur, Meerut 302 IPC, 3(2)5 SC/ST Act 3 188/2018 N/A Israna, Panipat 379-B, 34 IPC 4 187/2018 N/A Israna, Panipat 307, 379-B IPC, 25/54/59 of Arms Act 5 Dinesh vs State Of Haryana on 28 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/178304662/ 2 241/2018 N/A Ladwa, Kurukshetra 364-A, 395 IPC, 25/54/59 of Arms Act 6 699/2018 N/A City Rohtak, Rohtak 395, 397, 120-B IPC 7 66/2018 N/A Baroda, Sonipat 302-2(1) IPC, 6 POCSO Act, 307, 379-B, 120-B, 34 IPC 8 442/2018 N/A Murthal, Sonipat 307, 332, 353, 399, 402, 412, 420, 467, 468, 471 IPC 7.",
    "facts": "3. FIR was registered on the information supplied by Superintendent of Jail, Sonipat to Police Station Sonipat which reads as under : Dinesh vs State Of Haryana on 28 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/178304662/ 1 1 of 4 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:111096 \"xxxx On receiving information of this incident, other staff of jail reached the spot and right away took inmate Jagbir to hospital. From where it was informed that inmate Jagbir has died. In this incident, Head Warden Kadam Singh and Naveen Mandhori suffered injuries, their MLRS are attached alongwith.",
    "arguments": "4. Counsel for the petitioner submits that one of the eye-witnesses namely Kadam Singh who was examined as PW4 and also brother of the complainant has not attributed any role to the petitioner qua the deceased. 2 of 4 Neutral Citation No:=2024:PHHC:111096 He further submits that so far as the allegation levelled in the FIR against the petitioner is w.r.t. nabbing Naveen @ Mandhori and not w.r.t. the deceased. 5. I have heard counsel for the petitioner and have carefully gone through records of the case. 6. Bare perusal of the FIR reveals a gory incident that too within the jail premises. Even as per the allegations levelled in the present FIR, it is the petitioner who initiated the whole incident by nabbing Naveen @ Mandhori. Apart from these, State Counsel submits that the petitioner has earned two convictions as well."
  },
